From: Field Lab dependency spike
Subject: [PATCH] FastSIMD: limit MinGW assembler workaround to GNU

llvm-mingw uses Clang's integrated assembler, which rejects the GNU assembler
option -muse-unaligned-vector-move. The workaround is only applicable when the
compiler driver is GNU.

diff --git a/dispatch/cmake/ClassSIMD.cmake b/dispatch/cmake/ClassSIMD.cmake
--- a/dispatch/cmake/ClassSIMD.cmake
+++ b/dispatch/cmake/ClassSIMD.cmake
@@ -110,3 +110,3 @@ function(fastsimd_create_dispatch_library simd_library_name)
-    if(MINGW)
+    if(MINGW AND CMAKE_CXX_COMPILER_ID STREQUAL "GNU")
         target_compile_options(${simd_library_name} PRIVATE -Wa,-muse-unaligned-vector-move)
     endif()
